# =============================================================================
# mbsync Configuration — IMAP → Maildir Sync
# =============================================================================
# Image: ghcr.io/jakewharton/mbsync:latest
# Deploy this file to app-data/mbsync/config/mbsync.rc (the container reads
# /config/mbsync.rc). Emails sync into app-data/mbsync/data/ (/mail), which is
# mounted read-only into recoll-engine at /homes/mail for indexing.
#
# Four mailboxes are configured:
#   Alex:  alex-gmail (Gmail IMAP), alex-imap (generic IMAP)
#   Chloe: chloe-outlook (Outlook.com IMAP), chloe-imap (generic IMAP)
#
# Each has its own IMAPAccount + IMAPStore + MaildirStore + Channel.
# Maildirs are separate per account (Path /mail/<account>/).
#
# Password: mbsync does NOT expand ${VAR} in this file. PassCmd pulls the
# secret from the container environment at each sync — value never lands in
# the file or in /proc/<pid>/cmdline. Passwords are set in .env and passed
# through the compose `environment:` block.
#
# Username: no expansion either, so it is a literal below (not a secret).
# Replace each placeholder with the real mailbox login.
# =============================================================================

# ------------------------- Alex — Gmail IMAP --------------------------------
IMAPAccount alex-gmail
    Host imap.gmail.com
    Port 993
    User alex@gmail.com
    PassCmd "printenv IMAP_PASS_ALEX_GMAIL"
    AuthMechs LOGIN
    SSLType IMAPS
    PipelineDepth 50

IMAPStore alex-gmail-remote
    Account alex-gmail

MaildirStore alex-gmail-local
    Path /mail/alex-gmail/
    Inbox /mail/alex-gmail/INBOX
    SubFolders Verbatim

Channel alex-gmail-channel
    Far :alex-gmail-remote:
    Near :alex-gmail-local:
    Patterns INBOX INBOX.*
    Sync Pull
    Create Near
    Expunge Near
    SyncState *

